# Percentage addition relative to the left operand

Verifies a percentage on the right of addition reads as a fraction of the left operand. Adding decimal 50% to plain 100 returns the plain 150.00, while adding 10% to 8m preserves the meter unit with 8.80m.

>>> source
const total: decimal = 100
const rate: decimal = 50%
print(total + rate)
const length: decimal = 8m
const bonus: decimal = 10%
print(length + bonus)

<<< stdout
150.00
8.80m

<<< stderr
